1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,028
Detective Photon enters the crystal city with
one question: who stole the X-ray beam?

2
00:00:06,028 --> 00:00:12,248
Every atom is lined up in planes, like tiny
apartment floors made of electrons.

3
00:00:12,248 --> 00:00:18,420
One beam bounces from the top floor. Another
dives deeper, then bounces back.

4
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,944
The deeper beam walks an extra distance: two d
sine theta.

5
00:00:23,944 --> 00:00:29,180
If that extra walk is exactly n wavelengths, the
waves clap together.

6
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:37,920
That is Bragg's law: n lambda equals two d sine
theta. Mystery solved; diffraction peak
unlocked.
